    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0112" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/574: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-28T12:00:00-04:00">March 28,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>493. Further reference my 463, March 23; 474, March 24 and Department’s 337,
                    March 25.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d112-f1"/> To conserve gasoline stocks Chilean
                    pool committee March 25 reduced deliveries by distributing committees 20% and
                    recommended to Government immediate prohibition use private motorcar Sundays and
                    holidays but at Cabinet meeting March 27 this proposal rejected as too drastic.
                    Committee thereupon increased reduction gasoline deliveries to 25% and hopes
                    apply card rationing system about May 1. On basis reduced deliveries it is hoped
                    stocks will last until approximately April 20 whereas according to latest
                    information tanker <hi rendition="#italic">Svithiod</hi> delayed further 2 days
                    not arriving Valparaiso before April 15. As any further delay to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Svithiod</hi> would mean complete exhaustion gasoline
                    stocks, imperative that Department continue to do everything possible to hasten
                    arrival this vessel and also of additional tanker which I understand has been
                    allotted.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office officially notified March 28 consumption of all petroleum products
                    should be curtailed immediately by at least 15% and that necessity further
                    curtailment probable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
